      "question": "<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(z) = z^3 + pz^2 + qz - 15\"></span></p><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span> are real constants.</p><p>Given that the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(z) = 0\"></span> has roots</p><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha, \\frac{5}{\\alpha}\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(\\alpha + \\frac{5}{\\alpha} - 1\\right)\"></span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) solve completely the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(z) = 0\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Hence find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
