    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-sample/q4",
      "question": "<p>The cubic equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x^3 + 3x^2 - 8x + 6 = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>has roots <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha, \\beta\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\gamma\"></span>.</p><p>Without solving the equation, find the cubic equation whose roots are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\alpha - 1), (\\beta - 1)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\gamma - 1)\"></span>, giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w^3 + pw^2 + qw + r = 0\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p, q\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\"></span> are integers to be found.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
