    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-sample/q5",
      "question": "<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 &amp; -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} &amp; 1 \\end{pmatrix}\"></span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M\"></span> is non-singular.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>The hexagon <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> is transformed to the hexagon <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S\"></span> by the transformation represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M\"></span>.</p><p>Given that the area of hexagon <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> is 5 square units,</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) find the area of hexagon <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>The matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M\"></span> represents an enlargement, with centre <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0, 0)\"></span> and scale factor <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k &gt; 0\"></span>, followed by a rotation anti-clockwise through an angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\"></span> about <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0, 0)\"></span>.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(d) Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
