      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-sample/q6",
      "question": "<p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Prove by induction that for all positive integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span>,</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r^2 = \\frac{1}{6} n(n+1)(2n+1)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Use the standard results for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r^3\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r\"></span> to show that for all positive integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span>,</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r(r+6)(r-6) = \\frac{1}{4} n(n+1)(n-8)(n+9)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) Hence find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span> that satisfies</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r(r+6)(r-6) = 17 \\sum_{r=1}^{n} r^2\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
