    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-sample/q9",
      "question": "<p>An octopus is able to catch any fish that swim within a distance of 2 m from the octopus’s position.</p><p>A fish <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"F\"></span> swims from a point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> to a point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span>.</p><p>The octopus is modelled as a fixed particle at the origin <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span>.</p><p>Fish <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"F\"></span> is modelled as a particle moving in a straight line from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span>.</p><p>Relative to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span>, the coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-3, 1, -7)\"></span> and the coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(9, 4, 11)\"></span>, where the unit of distance is metres.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Use the model to determine whether or not the octopus is able to catch fish <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"F\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(7)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Criticise the model in relation to fish <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"F\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) Criticise the model in relation to the octopus.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
